[SHUSHES]

244
00:18:35,261 --> 00:18:38,430
Okay… I'm all yours.

245
00:18:50,984 --> 00:18:53,528
<i>My name is Helena, and I'm an Eagan.</i>
[LAUGHS]

246
00:18:55,238 --> 00:18:57,281
<i>So one of the things you
learn growing up as an Eagan</i>

247
00:18:57,365 --> 00:18:59,408
<i>is that the workers are our family.</i>

248
00:18:59,492 --> 00:19:01,410
<i>And I remember being
confused about that as a kid,</i>

249
00:19:01,494 --> 00:19:02,495
<i>because I thought that meant</i>

250
00:19:02,579 --> 00:19:04,997
<i>I had a few hundred thousand
literal brothers and sisters</i>

251
00:19:05,081 --> 00:19:07,416
<i>scattered around the world.</i> [CHUCKLES]

252
00:19:07,500 --> 00:19:08,626
<i>Oh, my God.</i>

253
00:19:09,294 --> 00:19:12,463
<i>But as I grew older, I learned
that it's about shared ideals.</i>

254
00:19:12,547 --> 00:19:13,797
<i>Um…</i> [CHUCKLES]

255
00:19:13,881 --> 00:19:16,634
<i>My dad used to make me
recite the nine core principles</i>

256
00:19:16,718 --> 00:19:17,885
<i>before bed every night,</i>

257
00:19:17,969 --> 00:19:20,804
<i>which I can't say I always did happily.
Sorry, Dad.</i>

258
00:19:20,888 --> 00:19:25,017
<i>But those are now the values that I
share with everyone who works at Lumon,</i>

259
00:19:25,101 --> 00:19:27,353
<i>and that's what makes them my family.</i>

260
00:19:27,979 --> 00:19:30,439
[ECHOING] <i>And I would never
ever ask them to do anything</i>

261
00:19:30,523 --> 00:19:33,442
<i>that I'm not willing or
excited to do myself.</i>

262
00:19:33,526 --> 00:19:36,737
[NORMAL VOICE] <i>Oh. Look, m-my
dad would love for me to sit here</i>

263
00:19:36,821 --> 00:19:39,323
<i>and say that I'm taking
this job out of loyalty</i>

264
00:19:39,407 --> 00:19:44,078
<i>and that it was the spirit of
pure Eagan calling me to service.</i>

265
00:19:44,787 --> 00:19:49,751
<i>But I took a severed job because
it sounds freaking awesome.</i>

266
00:19:50,543 --> 00:19:52,921
<i>So, no, I don't think
severance divides us.</i>

267
00:19:53,755 --> 00:19:55,256
<i>I think it brings us together.</i>

268
00:20:11,940 --> 00:20:13,775
[TIRES SQUEALING]

269
00:20:14,525 --> 00:20:15,526
MR. MILCHICK: <i>Greetings.</i>

270
00:20:15,610 --> 00:20:17,987
<i>-I'm not here right now.</i>
-Goddamn it, Milchick!

271
00:20:19,989 --> 00:20:21,449
[PAPERS SHUFFLING]

272
00:21:57,169 --> 00:22:00,172
[BREATHES HEAVILY]

273
00:22:08,930 --> 00:22:09,931
[DOOR OPENS]

274
00:22:11,098 --> 00:22:12,099
ASSISTANT: Helena.

275
00:22:12,767 --> 00:22:13,976
She's in here, sir.

276
00:22:24,237 --> 00:22:25,238
Helena.

277
00:22:28,199 --> 00:22:29,784
You look so nice.

278
00:22:32,662 --> 00:22:33,704
Like a film.

279
00:22:36,624 --> 00:22:37,625
HELLY: Thank you.

280
00:22:41,504 --> 00:22:42,505
Are you…

281
00:22:44,382 --> 00:22:46,384
Are you still in pain?

282
00:22:48,803 --> 00:22:49,804
I'm not.

283
00:22:51,013 --> 00:22:52,014
Not anymore.

284
00:22:58,771 --> 00:23:02,191
I cried in my bed when they told
me what she tried to do to you.

285
00:23:03,317 --> 00:23:05,903
What that innie tried to do. I…

286
00:23:09,782 --> 00:23:11,682
Thank you for going through with this.

287
00:23:13,202 --> 00:23:15,538
The Grandfather would
cherish what you've done.

288
00:23:17,456 --> 00:23:21,502
And one day you will sit
with me at my revolving.

289
00:23:25,172 --> 00:23:26,382
Are you feeling well?

290
00:23:27,883 --> 00:23:28,884
Yeah.

291
00:23:29,385 --> 00:23:33,806
I think, uh… I think the
drink just hit me a little bit.

292
00:23:35,558 --> 00:23:37,393
You'll be all right for the speech?

293
00:23:39,437 --> 00:23:41,564
For my speech. Yeah. Of course.

294
00:23:44,983 --> 00:23:48,153
Do you remember when I brought
home the first chip to show you?

295
00:23:50,614 --> 00:23:51,698
The prototype.

296
00:23:53,909 --> 00:23:56,244
It had the blue and
green lights back then.

297
00:23:58,121 --> 00:23:59,122
Yeah.

298
00:24:00,874 --> 00:24:04,961
I remember you said to
me, "It's so pretty, Daddy.

299
00:24:06,713 --> 00:24:09,257
Everybody in the whole
world should get one."

300
00:24:11,718 --> 00:24:12,761
They will.

301
00:24:15,513 --> 00:24:16,598
Because of you.

302
00:24:20,268 --> 00:24:22,062
They'll all be Kier's children.

303
00:24:22,604 --> 00:24:24,454
-[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]
-[DOOR OPENS]

304
00:24:25,565 --> 00:24:29,069
NATALIE: Mr. Eagan. Helena.
It's time to head to stage.

305
00:24:54,094 --> 00:24:58,473
[WHISPERS] Forgive me for
the harm I've caused this world.

306
00:25:00,433 --> 00:25:05,814
None may atone for my actions… but me.

307
00:25:09,234 --> 00:25:13,363
And only in me shall their stain live on.

308
00:25:17,033 --> 00:25:18,910
All I can be is sorry.

309
00:25:20,662 --> 00:25:22,288
And that is all I am.

310
00:25:42,600 --> 00:25:44,143
[SIGHS]

311
00:26:26,518 --> 00:26:28,145
[ENGINE STARTS]

312
00:26:44,078 --> 00:26:45,079
[TIRES SCREECH]

313
00:27:06,558 --> 00:27:08,708
DEVON: <i>You swear
you're not fucking with me?</i>

314
00:27:09,060 --> 00:27:10,061
I swear.

315
00:27:11,187 --> 00:27:13,063
This is so insane.

316
00:27:13,147 --> 00:27:15,983
They need to send people down
to check every inch of that place.

317
00:27:16,067 --> 00:27:19,570
Like, inspectors or whatever.
Is that a thing? Inspectors?

318
00:27:19,654 --> 00:27:21,197
Yeah. There are inspectors.

319
00:27:22,198 --> 00:27:23,908
Mark has b… I mean, out here,

320
00:27:23,992 --> 00:27:27,578
you have been trying to figure
out what Lumon does. What you do.

321
00:27:27,662 --> 00:27:28,663
Okay.

322
00:27:31,624 --> 00:27:32,625
I just…

323
00:27:34,669 --> 00:27:36,754
I just want to know why.

324
00:27:38,381 --> 00:27:40,383
Why he put me in there.

325
00:27:45,138 --> 00:27:47,140
[SIGHS] He lost his wife.

326
00:27:47,807 --> 00:27:51,227
You lost your wife.
A little before you started at Lumon.

327
00:27:52,353 --> 00:27:54,022
-Gemma.
-Mm-hmm.

328
00:27:55,523 --> 00:28:00,361
It was a car accident, and, at
first, you tried to keep teaching.

329
00:28:01,738 --> 00:28:03,030
I was a teacher?

330
00:28:03,114 --> 00:28:05,533
A professor. Of history.

331
00:28:05,617 --> 00:28:09,467
[INHALES SHARPLY] You tried to go back
to teaching three weeks after she died,

332
00:28:09,954 --> 00:28:12,624
and it was a disaster.

333
00:28:14,083 --> 00:28:16,920
She was just still in
your veins, you know?

334
00:28:17,462 --> 00:28:18,612
Making everything hurt.

335
00:28:20,673 --> 00:28:24,218
Which is why I guess you
thought the severed job would…

336
00:28:27,013 --> 00:28:29,015
He hoped you'd be spared from the pain.

337
00:28:38,273 --> 00:28:39,691
It's a nice name. Gemma.

338
00:28:39,775 --> 00:28:40,776
[DEVON CHUCKLES]

339
00:28:41,944 --> 00:28:44,071
[CHUCKLES] Yeah.

340
00:28:46,114 --> 00:28:48,825
We were all really close. It was great.

341
00:28:50,619 --> 00:28:51,912
She was wonderful.

342
00:28:53,413 --> 00:28:54,623
She made you wonderful.

343
00:29:29,533 --> 00:29:31,368
[TIRES SQUEALING]

344
00:29:39,126 --> 00:29:39,960
[RINGING]

345
00:29:43,088 --> 00:29:44,714
They told me not to talk to you.

346
00:29:44,798 --> 00:29:49,385
The goddamn OTC's been triggered!
Mark S. is his fucking innie!

347
00:29:49,469 --> 00:29:50,595
What? That's not possible.

348
00:29:50,679 --> 00:29:51,889
[TIRES SQUEALING]

349
00:29:52,556 --> 00:29:55,058
It's Dylan.
They've been plotting this all along.

350
00:29:55,142 --> 00:29:56,351
Helly's at the gala.

351
00:29:56,435 --> 00:30:00,272
I'll take care of Helly.
I'll fix it like I fix everything.

352
00:30:01,064 --> 00:30:04,692
Get to the security
office, and shut it off now!

353
00:30:04,776 --> 00:30:06,194
Shit!

354
00:30:23,127 --> 00:30:24,086
[BEEPS]

355
00:30:25,421 --> 00:30:27,298
Goddamn it! Dylan!

356
00:30:27,798 --> 00:30:28,674
Dylan!

357
00:30:29,717 --> 00:30:31,718
I know you're in there, Dylan.
Open the door!

358
00:30:31,802 --> 00:30:33,888
Fuck you, Mr. Milchick!

359
00:30:34,597 --> 00:30:37,058
Dylan! Dylan!

360
00:30:39,018 --> 00:30:40,936
Ricken knows a lot of
high-end journalists in New York.

361
00:30:41,020 --> 00:30:43,105
And you think that's
better than the police?

362
00:30:43,189 --> 00:30:45,732
Well, Lumon has their
hands in so many pies.

363
00:30:45,816 --> 00:30:47,401
Sorry, do you understand metaphor?

364
00:30:47,485 --> 00:30:49,236
Yeah, hands in pies. I get it.

365
00:30:49,320 --> 00:30:51,613
I think we have to be really
careful about who we talk to.

366
00:30:51,697 --> 00:30:53,490
-Okay.
-How much time do you have?

367
00:30:53,574 --> 00:30:55,242
I don't know. Maybe an hour?

368
00:30:55,326 --> 00:30:57,494
Right. Because once your bosses find out…

369
00:30:57,578 --> 00:31:01,415
Jesus, I totally forgot.
Cobel! Why is Cobel here?

370
00:31:01,499 --> 00:31:02,708
What?

371
00:31:02,792 --> 00:31:05,544
My boss from Lumon.
Ms. Cobel. She's at this party.

372
00:31:05,628 --> 00:31:06,753
What are you talking about?

373
00:31:06,837 --> 00:31:08,797
I mean, she's dressed different.

374
00:31:08,881 --> 00:31:11,884
Kind of a flowy,
purple outfit, silver hair.

375
00:31:13,261 --> 00:31:15,261
Mark, are you talking about Mrs. Selvig?

376
00:31:15,596 --> 00:31:17,932
Maybe, but her name is Harmony Cobel.

377
00:31:18,432 --> 00:31:20,100
And she works at Lumon?

378
00:31:20,184 --> 00:31:21,310
Yeah, she's my boss.

379
00:31:21,394 --> 00:31:22,562
Jesus fucking Christ.

380
00:31:50,673 --> 00:31:51,840
MR. MILCHICK: Dylan.

381
00:31:51,924 --> 00:31:53,324
Why are you doing this, man?

382
00:31:54,050 --> 00:31:55,051
Come on.

383
00:31:56,303 --> 00:31:58,846
You are the refiner of the quarter!

384
00:31:58,930 --> 00:32:01,682
RICKEN: "While most
cultures view sex as ugly or foul,

385
00:32:01,766 --> 00:32:03,267
-I've always seen it…"
-Mrs. Selvig?

386
00:32:03,351 --> 00:32:04,977
-What?
-Is she there? Is Mrs. Selvig there?

387
00:32:05,061 --> 00:32:05,895
-Do you…
-What?

388
00:32:05,979 --> 00:32:07,021
Mrs. Selvig?

389
00:32:07,105 --> 00:32:09,023
-What is going on?
-She has Eleanor!

390
00:32:09,107 --> 00:32:12,276
What? Um… Uh…
Excuse me a moment, okay. Um…

391
00:32:12,360 --> 00:32:14,779
Honey? What did you say?

392
00:32:14,863 --> 00:32:17,782
DEVON: Mrs. Selvig has Eleanor.
Did you see her?

393
00:32:20,744 --> 00:32:22,119
-Oh, my God.
-What is going on?

394
00:32:22,203 --> 00:32:23,955
Oh, my God. Her car's gone.

395
00:32:24,039 --> 00:32:26,374
I gave her the baby, and she left!

396
00:32:26,958 --> 00:32:29,210
-She left? With Eleanor?
-DEVON: I handed her the baby,

397
00:32:29,294 --> 00:32:30,294
and she left!

398
00:32:30,378 --> 00:32:32,296
-RICKEN: Have we looked everywhere?
-DEVON: Not yet!

399
00:32:32,380 --> 00:32:33,840
RICKEN: Okay, let's…
let's go inside and look.

400
00:32:33,924 --> 00:32:34,758
Oh, my God!

401
00:32:58,865 --> 00:33:02,285
[PANTING] I bet the
tempers were disappointed.

402
00:33:02,369 --> 00:33:04,120
I can still get you back in there.

403
00:33:04,621 --> 00:33:06,330
I can get you any perk you want, Dylan.

404
00:33:06,414 --> 00:33:09,250
Hey, there's stuff you
don't even know about.

405
00:33:09,334 --> 00:33:12,962
There's…
There's paintball, there's coffee cozies.

406
00:33:13,046 --> 00:33:14,297
Dylan, come on!

407
00:33:15,465 --> 00:33:18,551
Just say the word, and I'll get you a
coffee cozy literally right now, Dylan.

408
00:33:18,635 --> 00:33:19,677
Come on, man!

409
00:33:19,761 --> 00:33:23,431
I wanna remember my
fucking kid being born!

410
00:33:25,600 --> 00:33:27,269
You have two others.

411
00:33:28,478 --> 00:33:29,728
I can tell you about 'em.

412
00:33:30,981 --> 00:33:32,606
Open the door, and
I'll tell you their names.

413
00:33:32,690 --> 00:33:33,566
Come on, Dylan.

414
00:33:34,817 --> 00:33:36,867
-[BREATHES HEAVILY]
-MR. MILCHICK: Dylan!

415
00:33:48,414 --> 00:33:49,415
[TIRES SQUEALING]

416
00:33:51,125 --> 00:33:52,543
[TIRES SQUEALING]

417
00:34:08,809 --> 00:34:10,709
VALET: Whoa, whoa, whoa. It's rolling.

418
00:34:12,479 --> 00:34:15,900
HELLY: <i>My name is Helena,
and I'm an Eagan.</i> [CHUCKLES]

419
00:34:16,483 --> 00:34:20,153
<i>So one of the things you learn growing
up as an Eagan is that the workers…</i>

420
00:34:21,070 --> 00:34:23,156
-COORDINATOR: We start in two minutes.
-Thanks.

421
00:34:23,240 --> 00:34:24,240
Good luck.

422
00:34:25,951 --> 00:34:28,703
I'll tee you up.
Just stick to the talking points.

423
00:34:28,787 --> 00:34:31,705
Use the line about how you
see your innie as your sister.

424
00:34:31,789 --> 00:34:33,689
-They'll love that. [CHUCKLES]
-Got it.

425
00:34:34,251 --> 00:34:35,669
It's gonna be great.

426
00:35:21,005 --> 00:35:22,632
She's not in the baby room.

427
00:35:23,216 --> 00:35:24,926
Have all these rooms been checked?

428
00:35:26,010 --> 00:35:27,636
[ELEANOR CRYING]

429
00:35:27,720 --> 00:35:29,096
PATTON: Oh, thank God.

430
00:35:29,180 --> 00:35:30,682
Devon! I got her!

431
00:35:31,182 --> 00:35:34,310
Devon, she's here! I found her.

432
00:35:34,394 --> 00:35:35,812
I found your child.

433
00:35:36,980 --> 00:35:39,190
-I'm the one who found her!
-[CRYING FADES]

434
00:35:51,786 --> 00:35:52,912
MR. MILCHICK: Dylan!

435
00:35:55,081 --> 00:35:56,373
Dylan!

436
00:35:56,457 --> 00:35:57,625
NATALIE: <i>…improvements in morale,</i>

437
00:35:57,709 --> 00:35:59,709
-<i>a happier workplace.</i>
-[BREATHES HEAVILY]

438
00:36:00,628 --> 00:36:04,465
As with any transformative
technology, there have been setbacks.

439
00:36:04,549 --> 00:36:05,674
Bumps in the road.

440
00:36:05,758 --> 00:36:10,054
But I'm here tonight to tell you that
we are on the verge of a revolution.

441
00:36:10,138 --> 00:36:12,473
A kind and empathetic revolution

442
00:36:12,557 --> 00:36:13,974
that puts the human being…

443
00:36:14,058 --> 00:36:17,604
-Oh, my God! [BREATHES HEAVILY]
-Is it you?

444
00:36:18,271 --> 00:36:20,773
[STAMMERS] What are you talking about?

445
00:36:21,274 --> 00:36:24,693
[EXHALES SHARPLY] It is you, isn't it?

446
00:36:24,777 --> 00:36:29,073
-[BREATHES SHAKILY]
-I'm gonna kill your company.

447
00:36:29,157 --> 00:36:30,157
[MS. COBEL GASPS]

448
00:36:30,241 --> 00:36:31,659
Your company!

449
00:36:32,577 --> 00:36:35,162
Who the hell do you think you are?

450
00:36:35,246 --> 00:36:38,207
No. Your friends are gonna suffer.

451
00:36:39,208 --> 00:36:41,418
Mark will suffer.

452
00:36:41,502 --> 00:36:43,587
You'll be long gone,

453
00:36:43,671 --> 00:36:49,092
but we will keep them alive, in pain.

454
00:36:49,676 --> 00:36:50,844
You're on.

455
00:36:50,928 --> 00:36:53,263
NATALIE: …decided that we could do better.

456
00:36:53,347 --> 00:36:56,558
He may never have seen a
severance chip in his lifetime,

457
00:36:56,642 --> 00:37:01,354
but it represents his gentle and
elegant vision made manifest.

458
00:37:01,438 --> 00:37:05,088
<i>But why don't we hear from someone
who can tell us all about it firsthand?</i>

459
00:37:06,902 --> 00:37:09,362
<i>Ladies and gentlemen, our guest of honor,</i>

460
00:37:09,446 --> 00:37:11,657
Helena Eagan. [CHUCKLES]

461
00:37:18,455 --> 00:37:19,665
Thank you, Natalie.

462
00:37:25,295 --> 00:37:26,296
[GASPS]

463
00:37:50,362 --> 00:37:51,488
Devon!

464
00:37:56,118 --> 00:37:57,418
HELLY: <i>My name is Helly R.</i>

465
00:37:58,829 --> 00:38:00,080
I'm an innie.

466
00:38:01,748 --> 00:38:04,667
<i>And everything they've told
you about severance is a lie!</i>

467
00:38:04,751 --> 00:38:05,752
Devon!

468
00:38:08,255 --> 00:38:09,923
Burt!

469
00:38:11,383 --> 00:38:12,383
Burt!

470
00:38:12,467 --> 00:38:15,762
No, no, no. Listen, we're not happy.
We're miserable.

471
00:38:17,180 --> 00:38:18,640
Burt!

472
00:38:19,766 --> 00:38:23,437
-[GRUNTING, SCREAMING]
-They torture us down there!

473
00:38:24,021 --> 00:38:25,355
IRVING: <i>Burt!</i>

474
00:38:25,439 --> 00:38:27,899
Devon! Please!

475
00:38:29,025 --> 00:38:30,109
We're prisoners!

476
00:38:31,485 --> 00:38:33,279
She's alive!

477
00:38:33,779 --> 00:38:34,864
[DYLAN GRUNTS]

478
00:38:35,323 --> 00:38:36,324
Burt!

479
00:38:39,285 --> 00:38:40,620
[ELEVATOR BELL DINGS]

